{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798514-i-don-t-get-changeling","id":798514,"title":"I don't \"get\" Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-02T17:52:27-08:00","id":798514,"title":"I don't \"get\" Changeling","content":"Ok. Confession time. Way back, I bought Changeling, first edition. First impression was HOLY COLORS!!!!! I liked some elements, but the whole thing just didn't jive for me. For example: Banality. From what I remember, it means that modern stuff, even good modern stuff like medicine and the Internet, are Bad, while non science stuff is Good. And the True Fae. Not sure about them. More than anything, I just didn't understand the feel, the headspacei would need to be in. I feel like I SHOULD like C:tD. I dont think I get it enough to know for sure, and I'm not sure why.<br /> <br /> So, please help me! I love books like Neverwhere, which I think might be a little like Changeling. Someone break it down, nice and slow for me. What does changeling feel like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T18:04:20-08:00","id":798523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/798514-i-don-t-get-changeling#post798514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. Confession time. Way back, I bought Changeling, first edition. First impression was HOLY COLORS!!!!! I liked some elements, but the whole thing just didn't jive for me. For example: Banality. From what I remember, it means that modern stuff, even good modern stuff like medicine and the Internet, are Bad, while non science stuff is Good. And the True Fae. Not sure about them. More than anything, I just didn't understand the feel, the headspacei would need to be in. I feel like I SHOULD like C:tD. I dont think I get it enough to know for sure, and I'm not sure why.<br /> <br /> So, please help me! I love books like Neverwhere, which I think might be a little like Changeling. Someone break it down, nice and slow for me. What does changeling feel like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't think you 'got' it, but the first edition especially suffers from a confusion of themes and tone. Banality is best thought of as disbelief not science. Science can be Glamorous (see: Resurgence) and that's even in the first edition. It's more nuanced than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 01-02-2016, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T13:10:24-08:00","id":800702,"title":"","content":"Neverwhere's actually a pretty decent reference for a good middle-of-the-road headspace. Faerie Tale, by Raymond Feist, can work also. It's fae and dreams and imaginary friends... but it's twisted horrors and nightmares and things under your bed too. You can go Peter Pan. You can go Labyrinth. You can have a King Arthur feel, or you can go Nightmare on Elm Street. It's a pretty big sandbox. <br /> <br /> Banality has a lot of definitions, but a very simplistic one I personally keep coming back to over the years has been: &quot;it's all in how you approach things&quot;. Take, say, chemistry. Sitting in front of a chem set putting together a solution might bore you to tears... but your lab partner loves it and wants to make it a part of his life. Science is banal to you, but not to your lab partner. One half of a date might spend an entire opera on their phone, checking Facebook and playing Angry Birds, while the other is completely enthralled in the story and singing. Banality <i>can</i> be that &quot;meh&quot; you get when you're faced with something that doesn't interest or motivate you, in addition to narrow minds and active disbelief in magic and mystery and fantastic things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T16:46:32-08:00","id":800808,"title":"","content":"The 1969 moon landing - a moment of shared public awe and wonder at a scientific achievement - caused a surge of glamour so strong that it allowed some of the Faerie nobility to break through into the real world from the Dreaming. So no, science is not synonymous with banality.<br /> <br /> I think the key thing to remember is that glamous is about joy, inspiration, awe and wonder. Banality is the glum, derivative routine that destroys your dreams.<br /> <br /> If science is being used to inspire minds - to amaze people with the possibilities - it's a source of glamour. Say, kids learning about dinosaurs for the first time, or someone having their mind blown by the idea that quantum physics means particles can be in two places at once.<br /> <br /> If science is being used to shut down ideas and dreams - to close off possibilities and to reinstate the mundane - it's a source of banality. Say, a kid being pressured to take pre-med instead of music because their family is convinced they'll never make it as a composer and is pressuring them to go for a respectable profession. And yeah, honestly, this could probably also extend to debunking myths. Using science to explain that Bloody Mary won't actually appear in the mirror so you don't have to fear her is still weakening a dream and reinstating the muggle-world-view, so it's probably banal even if done in a well-meaning way.<br /> <br /> To an extent there is a conflict between science and the Dreaming and the world of Changeling, because Chimerical reality (i.e. reality that's partly made of dreams) is fundamentally absurd and contradictory to technology. The Dreaming and Changelings aren't discriminatory about the source of their wonder and glamour, and I'd say science is very well-equipped to inspire on that level (for instance, the moon landing as a canonical example of shared wonder that had a profound effect on the Dreaming). But science is also well-equipped to break down <i>other</i> sources of glamour, like belief in myths or superstitions. <b>ETA</b>: On the other hand the reverse has certainly also been true throughout history, for example Galileo's persecution at the hands of the Church who couldn't handle his amazing ideas about the universe. <br /> <br /> As to the personal aspect - science as something boring, or something someone's forced into at the expense of a preferred hobby...that's really more down to social context than anything. I gave an example of a musician forced to take pre-med, but it could as equally be a kid who dreams of being a star baseball player, but can't make Little League because he's being forced to go to the dreaded Piano Lessons with a terrifying Autumn Person teacher who raps his knuckles if each note isn't perfect.<br /> <br /> As Maggie C said - it's about approach. Is it inspiring dreams? Then it's glamorous. Is it killing dreams? Then it's banal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","user":"beccatoria","date":". 01-05-2016, 05:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T19:02:33-08:00","id":800872,"title":"","content":"We could do with an FAQ thread as a sticky, I think, to compile these common questions in one place. It'd be helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}